note rgate.om: the ng-a64 back-end gate (allocator and full pipeline). Run from the omega-mv root:
note seed/out/omc < seed/ng/a64/rgate.om > rgate && ./rgate, with stdin one line naming an existing scratch directory.
note 1. Build mkir (seed/ng/src/ir.om + seed/ng/a64/tests/mkir.om), ngcheck (seed/ng/sha256.om + seed/ng/ngcheck.om,
note    ng-ir's witness), ng (the units of seed/ng/ng.units, in order; their sha256s are ngbuild's check), ngas
note    (seed/ng/ngtxt.om + seed/ng/ngas.om) and ngrun (seed/ng/src/ir.om + seed/ng/ngrun.om) with seed/out/omc; ngrand
note    (seed/ng/src/ir.om + seed/ng/ngrand.om) is built at step 7.
note 2. For each fixture N of mkir: mkir writes its ΩIR, which ngcheck must accept (exit 0); ng compiles it with
note    `@ng a64` (save pairs) and with `@ng a64 split` (separate saves); each ELF runs. The omc build of
note    seed/ng/a64/tests/ref/N.om runs. Both ng statuses must equal the fixture's expected status (fixed below:
note    computed independently with Wolfram, or the trap code of the fixture's check) and omc's status its omc
note    expectation: the same, except tsum, where omc traps 6 (106) a million calls deep and ng's E loop shape has no
note    recursion (BEYOND_OMC, IR.md s7.9 and D9: trap 6 is compared only when both trap). The stdout of the split
note    run and of omc's run must equal the pairs run's byte for byte (bcopy writes 65536 bytes, sort four lines).
note 3. For each ngrun fixture (text tdx: ng-ir's run pairs seed/ng/tests/ir/x-*.oir without x-float, and
note    seed/ng/a64/tests/oir/*.oir: every check op with its trap code on narrow and 64-bit types, calls past eight
note    arguments, globals, loads and stores, block-parameter loops, the E loop shape, the bench kernels, SLICE values
note    and their checks; r-rot: u8 and u16 rotl/rotr, amounts past the width; r-s12: ngrand seed 12 shrunk to its
note    `rotr u8`, the first random refusal): ngas
note    assembles it, ngcheck accepts it, ngrun (the reference interpreter, D9) runs it; its status must be a
note    program's (not 125, an op outside ngrun) and both ng forms must exit with it and write its stdout and stderr
note    byte for byte.
note 4. Every BL target in each `@ng a64` ELF must be a multiple of 64 (function entries aligned, D13).
note 5. Mutants of seed/ng/src/a64.om, each one equal-length text change that must occur exactly once; ng is rebuilt
note    with it and every fixture runs with `@ng a64`. A mutant is caught when some fixture's status differs from
note    its expected (mkir) or ngrun's (ngrun fixtures) status (or ng refuses, or the program is killed after 30 s)
note    or a BL target is misaligned. Every mutant must be caught:
note    1 spill reload reads the next slot      2 values crossing a call may take caller-saved registers
note    3 live-out values end at the block start  4 parallel moves ignore pending reads (block-argument cycles)
note    5 callee-saved registers are never saved  6 frame of 4 bytes per slot (slots overlap the saves)
note    7 function entries aligned to 16 bytes, not 64
note    8 the E loop shape never matches (tsum recurses and traps 6)  9 the E tail site adds acc to itself, not a
note    10 chk.bounds compares i with len, not len - e (oob stores past g)  11 alloca zero-fills half its area (zf)
note    12 write passes off as the count (mem)  13 u64 loads read one byte (mem)  14 a frame above 4095 bytes drops
note    its LSL 12 part (the zero fill runs over the globals: mem)  15 i8 loads zero-extend (wid)
note    16 a wrong trap code: chk.divovf exits 102, not 101  17 stack parameters all read the first incoming slot
note    18 stack arguments are stored one slot low  19 a slice's length wire takes its offset, not n
note    20 block arguments of slice type keep the target's own length (a shrinking loop slice never shrinks)
note    21 slice offsets are not scaled by the element size (u32 and u64 slices start at the wrong element)
note    22 monons (host 109) selects on GE, not LT: a successful clock read returns 0 (h-mono exits 1, ngrun 7)
note    23 fill stores without scaling the index by the element size (f-fill and f-fills: u32/u16/u64 elements)
note    24 realns reads CLOCK_MONOTONIC (h-real: the reading must lie between 2023-11-14 and 2100 and exceed monons)
note    25 a u8 rotate's second copy shifts by 24, not 16 (bits 16..23 stay zero: r-rot)
note    26 a u16 rotate's copy shifts by 8, not 16 (it overlaps itself: r-rot; u8 stays right)
note 6. Front phase (needs ng-front's front.om in ng.units: `@ng front-ir`). For each source of text tfr (ng-ir's
note    x-*.om run pairs without x-float, and ng-front's integer bench kernels seed/ng/front/kernels/*.om at full size):
note    ng reads `@ng front-ir` and the source and must exit 0; ngcheck must accept its ΩIR; ng compiles that ΩIR with
note    `@ng a64` and `@ng a64 split` and both ELFs run; omc builds the same source and it runs. Both ng statuses must
note    equal omc's, both stdouts omc's byte for byte, and both stderrs omc's byte for byte, except that when omc's
note    stderr is exactly one line of decimal digits (OMC-EFF-2: the kernel's elapsed nanoseconds, different on every
note    run) ng's must be one such line too. Every BL target of the `@ng a64` ELF must be a multiple of 64.
note    For each source of text tfz (x-float and the linear kernel, f64: outside the a64 slice) front-ir and ngcheck
note    must accept and both a64 forms must refuse (exit 5); they are counted as refused, never as compared.
note    Negative control (text tfd): fib40's front-ir and a64 build against omc's build of
note    seed/ng/a64/tests/front/fib39.om must be sound (same statuses, ngcheck accepts, BL aligned) and must differ
note    in stdout (Wolfram: Fibonacci[39] = 63245986, Fibonacci[40] = 102334155); a comparison that cannot tell
note    those apart fails the gate.
note 7. Random phase (D9): for each seed k in 1..nrd, ngrand (ng-ir's generator: a ΩIR unit valid by construction from
note    seed k) writes the unit, which then goes through step 3's checks with ngrand's status in place of ngas's:
note    ngcheck accepts, ngrun's status is a program's, both ng forms exit with it and write its stdout and stderr byte
note    for byte, BL targets aligned. A refusal by ng fails the seed. Mutants do not run this phase. Negative control:
note    ngrun's run of seed 1 against the `@ng a64` ELF of seed 2 must be sound and differ in status or stdout.
note Output: one line per fixture and per mutant, then PASS or FAIL. Exit 0 PASS, 1 FAIL, 2 a step could not run.
om2

global mem uchar 16777216
global pb uchar 4096
global pn ulong 1
global sd uchar 1024
global sn ulong 1
global av uchar 4096
global ap ulong 2
global stb uchar 4
global ob uchar 65536
global on ulong 1
global ex ulong 16
global eo ulong 16
global rg ulong 4
global dq ulong 128
global fv ulong 16

note regions of mem: sources [0, 8 MiB), ΩIR [8, 12), ELF [12, 14), units [14, 15), stdin [15, 16)
const rir ulong 8388608
const relf ulong 12582912
const runit ulong 14680064
const rin ulong 15728640
note ngrun's stderr is kept at mem[rerr, rerr + 65536), after its stdout (savout keeps at most 983040 bytes)
const rerr ulong 15663104

text tx "seed/out/omc\nseed/ng/ng.units\nseed/ng/src/ir.om\nseed/ng/a64/tests/mkir.om\nseed/ng/a64/tests/ref/\n.om\n/ng.om\n/ng.bin\n/mkir.om\n/mkir.bin\n/fx.name\n/fx.ir\n/fx.in\n/fx.elf\n/ref.bin\n/run.out\n/run.err\nseed/ng/src/a64.om\n@ng a64\n@ng a64 split\n/build.err\nseed/ng/sha256.om\nseed/ng/ngcheck.om\n/ngcheck.om\n/ngcheck.bin\nseed/ng/ngtxt.om\nseed/ng/ngas.om\nseed/ng/ngrun.om\n/ngas.om\n/ngas.bin\n/ngrun.om\n/ngrun.bin\n.oir\n@ng front-ir\nseed/ng/ngrand.om\n/ngrand.om\n/ngrand.bin\n"
text tdx "seed/ng/tests/ir/x-bits\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-conv\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-divmin\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-fib\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-fuel\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-fuelok\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-hello\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-i8\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-index\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-indexok\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-ovf64\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-ovf64ok\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-remmin\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-shift\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-add-u8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-add-i16\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-add-i32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-add-u64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-sub-u8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-sub-i8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-sub-u32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-sub-i64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-mul-i8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-mul-u32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-mul-i64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-mul-u64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-neg-i8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-neg-u16\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-neg-i64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-divz-u8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-divz-u32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-divz-i64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-divovf-i8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-divovf-i32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-divovf-i64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-shl-i8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-shl-i16\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-shl-i32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-shl-i64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-shift-u8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-shift-i32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-shift-u32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-shift-u64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-conv-i64-u8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-conv-i32-u16\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-conv-u64-i64\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-conv-i64-i8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-conv-u8-i8\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-conv-i64-u32\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-bounds-n\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-bounds-e0\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-bounds-ld\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-slice-n\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-slice-off\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-fuel\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-true-1\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-true-9\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-true-10\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/c-true-13\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/wide\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/mem2\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/eloop\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/b-fib\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/b-bcopy\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/b-sort\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/s-slice\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/s-tb\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/s-te\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/s-ts\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/s-ts2\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/b-chacha\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/h-mono\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/f-fill\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/f-fills\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/h-real\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/r-rot\nseed/ng/a64/tests/oir/r-s12\n"
text tfx "fib\ndeep\npress\nrot\nck\nar\ntsum\nmem\noob\nzf\nwid\nbcopy\nsort\n"
text tmp "a6_ew a_ldrx s 31 sub get a_vsl w 1 0 0\nx = ne get a_vx w 0\nget a_lout add mul x lw i get a_ben x\nif not a6_isrc d\nif ge r 19\nf = mul 8 add get a_fs 4 n\nwhile ne and get a_cn 0 63 0 bound 16\nif ne get i_oop m 10\na6_tsum l a\na6_cmpk i sub l e\na6_movi 17 shr get a_asz k 4\na6_mvadd 2 a6_loc a6_arg o 4\nret a_ldrxr\na6_ew a_subxi 31 31 h 1 0\nconst a_lsbx ulong 82\na6_fx a_cbzx 15 add 1000 c\na6_ew a_ldrx d 17 j 0 0\na6_ew a_strx l 31 sub k 8 0 0\na6_mov 15 n\na6_mvadd a6_wloc a6_lw d a6_wloc a6_lw s\na6_ew a_addx 16 b f 0 a6_lsz e\na6_ew a_cselx 0 0 2 11 0\na6_ew a6_stf t x b 15 a6_sh1 t 0\nck = ulong 0\na6_ew a_orrx 16 16 16 0 16\na6_ew a_orrx 16 a a 0 w\n"
text tmr "a6_ew a_ldrx s 31 add get a_vsl w 0 0 0\nx = eq get a_vx w 9\nget a_lout add mul x lw i get a_bst x\nif not a6_isrc 0\nif ge r 99\nf = mul 4 add get a_fs 4 n\nwhile ne and get a_cn 0 15 0 bound 16\nif ne get i_oop m 99\na6_tsum l l\na6_cmpk i sub l 0\na6_movi 17 shr get a_asz k 5\na6_mvadd 2 a6_loc a6_arg o 3\nret a_ldrbr\na6_ew a_subxi 31 31 h 0 0\nconst a_lsbx ulong 81\na6_fx a_cbzx 15 add 1001 c\na6_ew a_ldrx d 17 0 0 0\na6_ew a_strx l 31 sub k 7 0 0\na6_mov 15 f\na6_mvadd a6_wloc a6_lw d a6_wloc a6_lw d\na6_ew a_addx 16 b f 0 a6_lsz 2\na6_ew a_cselx 0 0 2 10 0\na6_ew a6_stf t x b 15 a6_sh1 1 0\nck = ulong 1\na6_ew a_orrx 16 16 16 0 24\na6_ew a_orrx 16 a a 0 8\n"
text tmsg "a64 rgate: fixture\npairs\nsplit\nomc\nexpected\nmutant\ncaught\nMISSED\nPASS\nFAIL\ncannot run step\nfixtures ok\nmutants caught\nngcheck\nmisaligned\nomc-expected\nstdout-same\na64 rgate: ngrun-fixture\nngas\nngrun\nstderr-same\nngrun fixtures ok\na64 rgate: front\nfront-ir\nstderr-ok\nfront cases ok\na64 rgate: front-refused\na64 rgate: front-control (ng: fib40, omc: fib39)\nfront refused ok\nfront control differs\na64 rgate: random seed\nngrand\nrandom seeds ok\na64 rgate: random-control (ng: seed 2, ngrun: seed 1)\nrandom control differs\n"
text tfr "seed/ng/tests/ir/x-bits\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-conv\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-divmin\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-fib\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-fuel\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-fuelok\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-hello\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-i8\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-index\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-indexok\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-ovf64\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-ovf64ok\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-remmin\nseed/ng/tests/ir/x-shift\nseed/ng/front/kernels/arith\nseed/ng/front/kernels/branch\nseed/ng/front/kernels/leafcall\nseed/ng/front/kernels/fib38\nseed/ng/front/kernels/fib40\nseed/ng/front/kernels/isort\nseed/ng/front/kernels/sieve\nseed/ng/front/kernels/sort\nseed/ng/front/kernels/matmul\n"
text tfz "seed/ng/tests/ir/x-float\nseed/ng/front/kernels/linear\n"
text tfd "seed/ng/front/kernels/fib40\nseed/ng/a64/tests/front/fib39\n"

const nfx ulong 13
const ndx ulong 77
const nmut ulong 26
const nrd ulong 1000
const nfr ulong 23
const nfz ulong 2

note ---- text lines: line k of text t (0 tx, 1 tfx, 2 tmp, 3 tmr, 4 tmsg, 5 tdx, 6 tfr, 7 tfz, 8 tfd) ----
fn tlen t ulong to ulong
if eq t 0
ret len tx
end
if eq t 1
ret len tfx
end
if eq t 2
ret len tmp
end
if eq t 3
ret len tmr
end
if eq t 5
ret len tdx
end
if eq t 6
ret len tfr
end
if eq t 7
ret len tfz
end
if eq t 8
ret len tfd
end
ret len tmsg
end

fn tch t ulong i ulong to ulong
if eq t 0
ret ulong get tx i
end
if eq t 1
ret ulong get tfx i
end
if eq t 2
ret ulong get tmp i
end
if eq t 3
ret ulong get tmr i
end
if eq t 5
ret ulong get tdx i
end
if eq t 6
ret ulong get tfr i
end
if eq t 7
ret ulong get tfz i
end
if eq t 8
ret ulong get tfd i
end
ret ulong get tmsg i
end

note tline t k: start of line k of text t (lines end with a newline)
fn tline t ulong k ulong to ulong
i = ulong 0
j = ulong 0
while lt j k bound 256
while ne tch t i 10 bound 4096
i = add i 1
end
i = add i 1
j = add j 1
end
ret i
end

fn tend t ulong i ulong to ulong
e = i
while ne tch t e 10 bound 4096
e = add e 1
end
ret e
end

note ---- output ----
fn oput b ulong to void
n = get on 0
if lt n len ob
put ob n uchar b
put on 0 add n 1
end
end

fn oflush to void
n = get on 0
p = ulong 0
while lt p n bound 65536
k = write 1 ob p sub n p
if le k 0
p = n
else
p = add p ulong k
end
end
put on 0 0
end

fn otl t ulong k ulong to void
i = tline t k
e = tend t i
while lt i e bound 4096
oput tch t i
i = add i 1
end
end

fn omsg k ulong to void
otl 4 k
end

fn odec v ulong to void
d = ulong 1
while ge div v d 10 bound 20
d = mul d 10
end
x = v
while gt d 0 bound 20
oput add 48 div x d
x = rem x d
d = div d 10
end
end

fn okv k ulong v ulong to void
oput 32
omsg k
oput 32
odec v
end

fn fail k ulong to void
omsg 10
oput 32
odec k
oput 10
omsg 9
oput 10
oflush
exit 2
end

note ---- paths in pb ----
fn pclr to void
put pn 0 0
end

fn pb1 b ulong to void
n = get pn 0
if ge n len pb
fail 0
end
put pb n uchar b
put pn 0 add n 1
end

fn ptl t ulong k ulong to void
i = tline t k
e = tend t i
while lt i e bound 4096
pb1 tch t i
i = add i 1
end
end

fn pset k ulong to void
pclr
ptl 0 k
end

fn pscr k ulong to void
pclr
i = ulong 0
while lt i get sn 0 bound 1024
pb1 ulong get sd i
i = add i 1
end
ptl 0 k
end

note pref f: pb = seed/ng/a64/tests/ref/<fixture f>.om
fn pref f ulong to void
pset 4
ptl 1 f
ptl 0 5
end

note ---- files ----
fn openr to int
r = fopen pb 0 get pn 0 0 0
if lt r 0
fail 1
end
ret int r
end

note openw md: create or truncate pb for writing with mode md (O_WRONLY|O_CREAT|O_TRUNC = 577)
fn openw md int to int
r = fopen pb 0 get pn 0 577 md
if lt r 0
fail 2
end
ret int r
end

fn fclo fd int to void
r = fclose fd
end

note readin o c: all of file pb into mem at offset o (capacity c bytes); returns the byte count
fn readin o ulong c ulong to ulong
fd = openr
n = ulong 0
go = true
while go bound 1000000
if ge n c
fail 3
end
k = read fd mem add o n sub c n
if lt k 0
fail 3
end
if eq k 0
go = false
else
n = add n ulong k
end
end
fclo fd
ret n
end

fn wall fd int o ulong n ulong to void
p = ulong 0
while lt p n bound 1000000
k = write fd mem add o p sub n p
if le k 0
fail 4
end
p = add p ulong k
end
end

note wtl fd t k: line k of text t and a newline to fd (staged at mem[rin])
fn wtl fd int t ulong k ulong to void
i = tline t k
e = tend t i
n = ulong 0
while le add i n e bound 4096
put mem add rin n uchar tch t add i n
n = add n 1
end
wall fd rin n
end

note ---- children: av = u16 count, then per argument u16 length and its bytes ----
fn aclr to void
put ap 0 2
put ap 1 0
end

fn apb to void
n = get pn 0
p = get ap 0
if gt add add p n 2 len av
fail 5
end
put av p uchar and n 255
put av add p 1 uchar shr n 8
i = ulong 0
while lt i n bound 4096
put av add add p 2 i get pb i
i = add i 1
end
put ap 0 add add p 2 n
put ap 1 add get ap 1 1
end

fn redir s int d int to void
if ne s d
if ne dupfd s d 0 long d
exit 127
end
end
end

note spawn fi fo fe: run av with stdin, stdout, stderr fi, fo, fe; returns the exit status, 256 + signal, and kills
note the child (status 265) when it runs longer than 30 s
fn spawn fi int fo int fe int to ulong
put av 0 uchar and get ap 1 255
put av 1 uchar shr get ap 1 8
pid = fork
if lt pid 0
fail 6
end
if eq pid 0
redir fi 0
redir fo 1
redir fe 2
r = execprog av 0 get ap 0
exit 127
end
fclo fi
fclo fo
fclo fe
ret reap pid
end

fn reap pid long to ulong
t0 = monons
while true bound 1000000
r = waitpid int pid stb 0 len stb 1
if eq r pid
ret wstat
end
if ne r 0
fail 7
end
if gt sub monons t0 30000000000
k = killpid int pid 9
end
s = sleepns 1000000
end
fail 7
ret 0
end

fn wstat to ulong
sg = and ulong get stb 0 127
if ne sg 0
ret add 256 sg
end
ret ulong get stb 1
end

note ---- building ----
note unitpath p q: pb = the path of the ng.units line mem[p, q) (`HEX PATH`, 64 hex digits and one space)
fn unitpath p ulong q ulong to void
if or le q add p 65 ne get mem add p 64 32
fail 17
end
pclr
i = add p 65
while lt i q bound 4096
pb1 ulong get mem i
i = add i 1
end
end

fn isa64 to bool
i = tline 0 17
e = tend 0 i
if ne get pn 0 sub e i
ret false
end
j = ulong 0
while lt j sub e i bound 64
if ne ulong get pb j tch 0 add i j
ret false
end
j = add j 1
end
ret true
end

note mkmut o n m: replace the one occurrence of mutant line m of tmp in mem[o, o+n) by line m of tmr
fn mkmut o ulong n ulong m ulong to void
p = tline 2 m
pl = sub tend 2 p p
r = tline 3 m
if ne pl sub tend 3 r r
fail 8
end
hits = ulong 0
hit = ulong 0
i = o
while le add i pl add o n bound 4194304
if samepat i p pl
hits = add hits 1
hit = i
end
i = add i 1
end
if ne hits 1
fail 8
end
j = ulong 0
while lt j pl bound 128
put mem add hit j uchar tch 3 add r j
j = add j 1
end
end

fn samepat i ulong p ulong pl ulong to bool
j = ulong 0
while lt j pl bound 128
if ne ulong get mem add i j tch 2 add p j
ret false
end
j = add j 1
end
ret true
end

note srcng m: the units of ng.units concatenated at mem[0); mutant m (1..) applied to a64.om, 0 none; the length
fn srcng m ulong to ulong
pset 1
nu = readin runit 1048576
s = ulong 0
p = runit
e = add runit nu
hit = ulong 0
while lt p e bound 128
q = untilnl p e
unitpath p q
k = readin s sub rir s
if and gt m 0 isa64
mkmut s k sub m 1
hit = add hit 1
end
s = add s k
p = add q 1
end
if and gt m 0 ne hit 1
fail 8
end
ret s
end

fn untilnl p ulong e ulong to ulong
q = p
while lt q e bound 4096
if eq get mem q 10
ret q
end
q = add q 1
end
ret q
end

note compile mem[0, n) with omc: scratch text s (source) -> scratch text b (binary); omc must succeed
fn omcb n ulong s ulong b ulong to void
pscr s
fd = openw 420
wall fd 0 n
fclo fd
pscr s
fi = openr
pscr b
fo = openw 493
pscr 20
fe = openw 420
aclr
pset 0
apb
if ne spawn fi fo fe 0
fail 9
end
end

fn buildng m ulong to void
omcb srcng m 6 7
end

fn buildmk to void
pset 2
n = readin 0 rir
pset 3
n = add n readin n sub rir n
omcb n 8 9
end

fn buildck to void
pset 21
n = readin 0 rir
pset 22
n = add n readin n sub rir n
omcb n 23 24
end

note runck: ngcheck.bin < fx.ir; its exit status (0 accept, else the refusal class)
fn runck to ulong
pscr 11
fi = openr
pscr 15
fo = openw 420
pscr 16
fe = openw 420
aclr
pscr 24
apb
ret spawn fi fo fe
end

note ---- running a fixture ----
note mkfx f: scratch/fx.name = fixture f's name; mkir.bin < fx.name > fx.ir; returns the ΩIR byte count (at rir)
fn mkfx f ulong to ulong
pscr 10
fd = openw 420
wtl fd 1 f
fclo fd
pscr 10
fi = openr
pscr 11
fo = openw 420
pscr 16
fe = openw 420
aclr
pscr 9
apb
if ne spawn fi fo fe 0
fail 11
end
pscr 11
ret readin rir 4194304
end

note runng n md: fx.in = mode line md (18 pairs, 19 split) + the ΩIR at rir (n bytes); ng.bin < fx.in > fx.elf;
note returns the program's status, or 1000 + ng's exit status when ng refuses
fn runng n ulong md ulong to ulong
pscr 12
fd = openw 420
wtl fd 0 md
wall fd rir n
fclo fd
pscr 12
fi = openr
pscr 13
fo = openw 493
pscr 16
fe = openw 420
aclr
pscr 7
apb
c = spawn fi fo fe
if ne c 0
ret add 1000 c
end
ret runbin 13
end

note runbin k: run scratch text k with stdin fx.name, stdout run.out, stderr run.err; its status
fn runbin k ulong to ulong
pscr 10
fi = openr
pscr 15
fo = openw 420
pscr 16
fe = openw 420
aclr
pscr k
apb
ret spawn fi fo fe
end

fn runref f ulong to ulong
pref f
n = readin 0 rir
omcb n 8 14
ret runbin 14
end

note ---- main ----
fn rdscr to void
pclr
n = read 0 mem rin 4096
if le n 0
fail 16
end
i = ulong 0
while lt i ulong n bound 4096
if eq get mem add rin i 10
i = add i 4096
else
put sd i get mem add rin i
i = add i 1
end
end
if ge i 4096
i = sub i 4096
end
if or eq i 0 ge i 1000
fail 16
end
put sn 0 i
end

fn expect f ulong to ulong
ret get ex f
end

note blbad: the number of BL instructions in scratch/fx.elf (code from byte 176) whose target is not a multiple of 64
fn blbad to ulong
pscr 13
m = readin relf 2097152
c = ulong 0
pc = ulong 176
while le add pc 4 m bound 524288
w = le32 add relf pc
if eq and w 0xfc000000 0x94000000
if ne and bltgt pc and w 0x3ffffff 63 0
c = add c 1
end
end
pc = add pc 4
end
ret c
end

fn le32 o ulong to ulong
v = ulong get mem o
v = or v shl ulong get mem add o 1 8
v = or v shl ulong get mem add o 2 16
ret or v shl ulong get mem add o 3 24
end

note bltgt pc i: target byte offset of a BL at pc with imm26 i (signed, in words)
fn bltgt pc ulong i ulong to ulong
if ge i 0x2000000
ret sub pc mul 4 sub 0x4000000 i
end
ret add pc mul 4 i
end

note savout: scratch run.out into mem[runit] (the units region is used only while building ng); its byte count
fn savout to ulong
pscr 15
ret readin runit 983040
end

note saverr: scratch run.err into mem[rerr]; its byte count
fn saverr to ulong
pscr 16
ret readin rerr 65536
end

note samef k b n: scratch text k (read into the staging region mem[rin]) equals the n bytes kept at mem[b]
fn samef k ulong b ulong n ulong to bool
pscr k
m = readin rin 1048576
if ne m n
ret false
end
i = ulong 0
while lt i n bound 1048576
if ne get mem add b i get mem add rin i
ret false
end
i = add i 1
end
ret true
end

note ---- ngrun fixtures: ΩIR text through ngas and ngcheck; ngrun (IR.md s7, the D9 oracle) against both ng forms ----
note pdx d: pb = the text file of ngrun fixture d (its line of tdx and .oir)
fn pdx d ulong to void
pclr
ptl 5 d
ptl 0 32
end

fn buildas to void
pset 25
n = readin 0 rir
pset 26
n = add n readin n sub rir n
omcb n 28 29
end

fn buildrun to void
pset 2
n = readin 0 rir
pset 27
n = add n readin n sub rir n
omcb n 30 31
end

note dxas d: ngas.bin < fixture d's text > fx.ir; ngas's status
fn dxas d ulong to ulong
pdx d
fi = openr
pscr 11
fo = openw 420
pscr 16
fe = openw 420
aclr
pscr 29
apb
ret spawn fi fo fe
end

note dxir d: fixture d's ΩIR at rir (its byte count), 0 bytes when ngas refuses; s gets ngas's status in rg[0]
fn dxir d ulong to ulong
s = dxas d
put rg 0 s
if ne s 0
ret 0
end
pscr 11
ret readin rir 4194304
end

note runrun: ngrun.bin fx.ir with stdin fx.name, stdout run.out, stderr run.err; its status
fn runrun to ulong
pscr 10
fi = openr
pscr 15
fo = openw 420
pscr 16
fe = openw 420
aclr
pscr 31
apb
pscr 11
apb
ret spawn fi fo fe
end

note ngrun fixture d: ngas and ngcheck accept it; ngrun's status (kept in dq for the mutants) is a program's (below
note 256) and not 125 (an op outside ngrun); both ng forms exit with it and write its stdout and stderr byte for byte;
note the `@ng a64` ELF has every BL target aligned to 64
fn dxrun d ulong to bool
n = dxir d
omsg 17
oput 32
otl 5 d
ok = dxcmp n 18
put dq d get rg 2
ret ok
end

note dxcmp n k: the ΩIR at rir (n bytes; its producer's status in rg[0], printed under message k) through ngcheck,
note ngrun and both ng forms with dxrun's verdict; prints the rest of the line; ngrun's status in rg[2]
fn dxcmp n ulong k ulong to bool
s = get rg 0
c = runck
q = runrun
put rg 2 q
o1 = savout
e1 = saverr
a = runng n 18
so = samef 15 runit o1
se = samef 16 rerr e1
al = blbad
b = runng n 19
so = and so samef 15 runit o1
se = and se samef 16 rerr e1
dxmsg k s c q a al
okv 2 b
okv 16 bv so
okv 20 bv se
oput 10
oflush
ok = and eq s 0 eq c 0
ok = and ok and ne q 125 lt q 256
ok = and ok and eq a q eq b q
ret and ok and and so se eq al 0
end

fn dxmsg k ulong s ulong c ulong q ulong a ulong al ulong to void
okv k s
okv 13 c
okv 19 q
okv 1 a
okv 14 al
end

fn bv b bool to ulong
if b
ret 1
end
ret 0
end

note fixture f: ngcheck accepts its ΩIR; both ng forms and the omc reference give the expected status, and the
note split and omc stdout equal the pairs stdout; the `@ng a64` ELF has every BL target aligned to 64
fn fxrun f ulong to bool
n = mkfx f
c = runck
a = runng n 18
o1 = savout
al = blbad
b = runng n 19
so = samef 15 runit o1
r = runref f
so = and so samef 15 runit o1
e = expect f
eom = get eo f
omsg 0
oput 32
otl 1 f
okv 13 c
okv 1 a
okv 14 al
okv 2 b
okv 3 r
okv 4 e
okv 15 eom
okv 16 bv so
oput 10
oflush
ok = and eq a e eq b e
ok = and ok and eq r eom so
ret and ok and eq c 0 eq al 0
end

note mutant m (1..): rebuild ng with it; caught when some fixture's `@ng a64` status differs from the expected one
note (mkir fixtures) or from ngrun's (ngrun fixtures), or a BL target is misaligned
fn mutrun m ulong to bool
buildng m
c = ulong 0
f = ulong 0
while lt f nfx bound 16
n = mkfx f
s = runng n 18
bb = blbad
if or ne s expect f gt bb 0
c = add c 1
end
f = add f 1
end
d = ulong 0
while lt d ndx bound 128
n = dxir d
s = runng n 18
bb = blbad
if or ne s get dq d gt bb 0
c = add c 1
end
d = add d 1
end
omsg 5
oput 32
odec m
oput 32
if gt c 0
omsg 6
else
omsg 7
end
oput 32
odec c
oput 10
oflush
ret gt c 0
end

note ---- front phase: Omega source -> @ng front-ir -> ngcheck -> both a64 forms, against omc on a source ----
note frsrc t k: line k of text t and ".om" read to mem[0); its byte count
fn frsrc t ulong k ulong to ulong
pclr
ptl t k
ptl 0 5
ret readin 0 rir
end

note frir t k: fx.in = the `@ng front-ir` line and source (t, k); ng.bin < fx.in > fx.ir; ng's status in rg[1]; the
note ΩIR at rir (its byte count; 0 when ng refuses)
fn frir t ulong k ulong to ulong
n = frsrc t k
pscr 12
fd = openw 420
wtl fd 0 33
wall fd 0 n
fclo fd
pscr 12
fi = openr
pscr 11
fo = openw 420
pscr 16
fe = openw 420
aclr
pscr 7
apb
s = spawn fi fo fe
put rg 1 s
if ne s 0
ret 0
end
pscr 11
ret readin rir 4194304
end

note frref t k: omc builds source (t, k) into ref.bin, which runs (runbin); its status
fn frref t ulong k ulong to ulong
n = frsrc t k
omcb n 8 14
ret runbin 14
end

note tmline b n: mem[b, b + n) is one line of decimal digits (OMC-EFF-2, a bench kernel's elapsed nanoseconds)
fn tmline b ulong n ulong to bool
if lt n 2
ret false
end
if ne get mem add b sub n 1 10
ret false
end
i = ulong 0
while lt i sub n 1 bound 65536
c = ulong get mem add b i
if or lt c 48 gt c 57
ret false
end
i = add i 1
end
ret true
end

note errok e1: scratch run.err equals the e1 bytes kept at mem[rerr], or both are one timing line
fn errok e1 ulong to bool
if samef 16 rerr e1
ret true
end
if not tmline rerr e1
ret false
end
pscr 16
m = readin rin 65536
ret tmline rin m
end

note frrun t k u j h: front-ir of source (t, k) through ngcheck and both a64 forms against omc's build of source
note (u, j); one output line headed by message h. 0 when all agree; 1 when the pipeline is sound (ng exits 0,
note ngcheck accepts, both statuses equal omc's, BL targets aligned) but stdout or stderr differs; 2 otherwise
fn frrun t ulong k ulong u ulong j ulong h ulong to ulong
put fv 0 frref u j
put fv 1 savout
put fv 2 saverr
frcmp frir t k
frout t k h
ret frverd
end

note frcmp n: the comparisons for the n ΩIR bytes at rir into fv: 3 ng's status, 4 ngcheck's, 5 pairs, 6 split,
note 7 stdout same, 8 stderr same (or both one timing line), 9 misaligned BL targets (omc's status in fv 0, its
note stdout and stderr byte counts in fv 1 and 2)
fn frcmp n ulong to void
s = get rg 1
put fv 3 s
put fv 4 99
put fv 5 9999
put fv 6 9999
put fv 7 0
put fv 8 0
put fv 9 0
if ne s 0
ret
end
put fv 4 runck
put fv 5 runng n 18
so = samef 15 runit get fv 1
se = errok get fv 2
put fv 9 blbad
put fv 6 runng n 19
so = and so samef 15 runit get fv 1
se = and se errok get fv 2
put fv 7 bv so
put fv 8 bv se
end

fn frout t ulong k ulong h ulong to void
omsg h
oput 32
otl t k
okv 23 get fv 3
okv 13 get fv 4
okv 1 get fv 5
okv 14 get fv 9
okv 2 get fv 6
okv 3 get fv 0
okv 16 get fv 7
okv 24 get fv 8
oput 10
oflush
end

fn frverd to ulong
r = get fv 0
ok = and and eq get fv 3 0 eq get fv 4 0 eq get fv 9 0
if not and ok and eq get fv 5 r eq get fv 6 r
ret 2
end
if and eq get fv 7 1 eq get fv 8 1
ret 0
end
ret 1
end

note frzero t k: a float source: front-ir exits 0, ngcheck accepts, both a64 forms refuse (exit 5); one output line
fn frzero t ulong k ulong to bool
n = frir t k
s = get rg 1
c = ulong 99
a = ulong 0
b = ulong 0
if eq s 0
c = runck
a = runng n 18
b = runng n 19
end
omsg 26
oput 32
otl t k
okv 23 s
okv 13 c
okv 1 a
okv 2 b
oput 10
oflush
ret and and eq s 0 eq c 0 and eq a 1005 eq b 1005
end

fn main to int
rdscr
put ex 0 17
put ex 1 106
put ex 2 198
put ex 3 191
put ex 4 101
put ex 5 245
put ex 6 32
put ex 7 163
put ex 8 103
put ex 9 0
put ex 10 209
put ex 11 0
put ex 12 0
f = ulong 0
while lt f nfx bound 16
put eo f get ex f
f = add f 1
end
put eo 6 106
buildmk
buildck
buildng 0
buildas
buildrun
okf = ulong 0
f = ulong 0
while lt f nfx bound 16
if fxrun f
okf = add okf 1
end
f = add f 1
end
okd = ulong 0
d = ulong 0
while lt d ndx bound 128
if dxrun d
okd = add okd 1
end
d = add d 1
end
frphase
rdphase
okm = ulong 0
m = ulong 1
while le m nmut bound 32
if mutrun m
okm = add okm 1
end
m = add m 1
end
omsg 11
oput 32
odec okf
oput 47
odec nfx
oput 10
omsg 21
oput 32
odec okd
oput 47
odec ndx
oput 10
put fv 13 bv and frsum rdsum
omsg 12
oput 32
odec okm
oput 47
odec nmut
oput 10
if and eq get fv 13 1 and and eq okf nfx eq okd ndx eq okm nmut
omsg 8
oput 10
oflush
ret 0
end
omsg 9
oput 10
oflush
ret 1
end

note frphase: the front phase; front cases ok in fv 10, refused float sources in fv 11, the control (1: the
note fib40 / fib39 comparison is sound and differs) in fv 12
fn frphase to void
okr = ulong 0
k = ulong 0
while lt k nfr bound 64
if eq frrun 6 k 6 k 22 0
okr = add okr 1
end
k = add k 1
end
put fv 10 okr
okz = ulong 0
k = ulong 0
while lt k nfz bound 8
if frzero 7 k
okz = add okz 1
end
k = add k 1
end
put fv 11 okz
put fv 12 bv eq frrun 8 0 8 1 27 1
end

note frsum: the front phase's three summary lines; true when every case agreed, both floats were refused and the
note control differed
fn frsum to bool
omsg 25
oput 32
odec get fv 10
oput 47
odec nfr
oput 10
omsg 28
oput 32
odec get fv 11
oput 47
odec nfz
oput 10
omsg 29
oput 32
odec get fv 12
oput 10
ret and and eq get fv 10 nfr eq get fv 11 nfz eq get fv 12 1
end

note ---- random phase (step 7): ngrand's seeded ΩIR (ng-ir, D9) against ngrun in both ng forms ----
fn buildrd to void
pset 2
n = readin 0 rir
pset 34
n = add n readin n sub rir n
omcb n 35 36
end

note pdec v: the decimal digits of v appended to pb
fn pdec v ulong to void
d = ulong 1
while ge div v d 10 bound 20
d = mul d 10
end
x = v
while gt d 0 bound 20
pb1 add 48 div x d
x = rem x d
d = div d 10
end
end

note rdir k: ngrand.bin k > fx.ir (stdin fx.name, stderr run.err); ngrand's status in rg[0]; the ΩIR at rir (its
note byte count, 0 when ngrand fails)
fn rdir k ulong to ulong
pscr 10
fi = openr
pscr 11
fo = openw 420
pscr 16
fe = openw 420
aclr
pscr 36
apb
pclr
pdec k
apb
s = spawn fi fo fe
put rg 0 s
if ne s 0
ret 0
end
pscr 11
ret readin rir 4194304
end

note rdphase: seeds 1..nrd, each with dxrun's verdict (ngrand's status in place of ngas's); the number of seeds that
note pass in fv 14, the control in fv 15
fn rdphase to void
buildrd
ok = ulong 0
k = ulong 1
while le k nrd bound 4096
n = rdir k
omsg 30
oput 32
odec k
if dxcmp n 31
ok = add ok 1
end
k = add k 1
end
put fv 14 ok
put fv 15 bv rdctl
end

note rdctl: the comparison tells programs apart: ngrun's run of seed 1 against the `@ng a64` ELF of seed 2 must be
note sound (ngrand and ngcheck accept both, ngrun's and the ELF's statuses are a program's) and differ in status or
note stdout
fn rdctl to bool
n = rdir 1
s = get rg 0
c = runck
q = runrun
o1 = savout
n = rdir 2
s = or s get rg 0
c = or c runck
a = runng n 18
so = samef 15 runit o1
omsg 33
okv 19 q
okv 1 a
okv 16 bv so
oput 10
oflush
ok = and and eq s 0 eq c 0 and lt q 256 lt a 256
ret and ok or ne a q not so
end

fn rdsum to bool
omsg 32
oput 32
odec get fv 14
oput 47
odec nrd
oput 10
omsg 34
oput 32
odec get fv 15
oput 10
ret and eq get fv 14 nrd eq get fv 15 1
end
